00:33:21,707 --> 00:33:25,889
The time scale is of course the annotated history of the planet,

596
00:33:25,989 --> 00:33:30,811
which we have broken down into time periods that basically to help us talk about it.

597
00:33:31,612 --> 00:33:35,954
And so now we present to you a really quick overview of the history of the planet.

598
00:33:36,014 --> 00:33:38,895
This is a whirlwind tour of the geologic time scale.

599
00:33:39,185 --> 00:33:44,027
At the beginning of the time scale, we start with a time period called the Hadean Eon.

600
00:33:44,407 --> 00:33:47,629
And Eon is a word that means a really, really long period of time.

601
00:33:47,909 --> 00:33:53,672
The Hadean Eon is a time that is identified by the fact that it doesn't seem like a great place to live.

602
00:33:53,712 --> 00:33:59,174
The crust is still forming, you're still getting bombarded by lots and lots of impacts,

603
00:33:59,526 --> 00:34:04,148
extraterrestrial impacts, no living organisms are known from this time.

604
00:34:04,468 --> 00:34:08,950
It is followed up by the Archaean Eon, which is notable for having fossils.

605
00:34:09,010 --> 00:34:15,212
The first fossils show up here, things like stromatolites, things that are hints at microbial life.

606
00:34:15,613 --> 00:34:22,856
We do actually find fossilized cells as well as the chemical residues of ancient life.

607
00:34:23,326 --> 00:34:27,728
Following that you have the Proterozoic Eon, which is another very long period of time,

608
00:34:27,808 --> 00:34:31,129
during which we see things like the rise of complex cells,

609
00:34:31,769 --> 00:34:37,792
the rise of photosynthesis, you know, cyanobacteria, organisms using photosynthesis.

610
00:34:38,272 --> 00:34:42,594
All throughout these three eons, life is microbial, life is simple,

611
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:48,276
the planet is not particularly very recognizable compared to today.

612
00:34:49,245 --> 00:34:53,147
The final eon of Earth history is the Phanerozoic.

613
00:34:53,247 --> 00:34:57,529
The Phanerozoic Eon starts with the event we talked about a couple episodes ago,

